      "writtenOn": "2021-06-04T18:38:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I didn\u0027t realize that this has to work with both old and new kernels.\nIt should be straightforward to modify this code to work with both. After all, the EC error code is still returned in s_cmd-\u003eresult. Instead of mapping errno back to the EC error code, it would be simpler to just use that error code. Something like \"if (s_cmd-\u003eresult !\u003d 0xff) rc \u003d -EECRESULT - s_cmd-\u003eresult;\" should do it (since s_cmd-\u003eresult was initialized with 0xff above).",
      "parentUuid": "f22a1393_d92fb21f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 193,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 193,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "cba489bd6b88604ec359a51c2d544e866a05cd64",
